  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This knitted sun hat is worked bottom-up in the round with a wide 10 cm brim picked up and increased outward from the cast-on edge, fitting adult heads of 54 (56, 58) cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bottom-up construction -- crown first, brim last -- means the brim can be tried as you work it and stopped at the desired projection. Cotton DK is chosen over wool because it holds a stiff, structural brim better than elastic wool fibres; the brim will not sag in warm weather. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " method works both crown and brim on one needle. About 120 g (265 m) of cotton DK. Brim sits level at the brow and shades the face and neck."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK-weight cotton or linen-blend yarn",
              "qty": "120 g (approx. 265 m)",
              "substitutions": "Cotton holds brim shape best"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 8 / US 6)",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "3.5 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 9 / US 4) -- for cast-on and brim edge",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "9 (1 BOR + 8 crown sections)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle and scissors",
              "qty": "1 each",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "22 sts x 30 rounds = 10 x 10 cm in stocking stitch on 4 mm needles, blocked. At 23 sts per 10 cm the crown fits 2 cm tighter at the brow; for a sun hat with a rigid brim this is more noticeable than on a stretchy beanie. Swatch in the round and measure before blocking and after."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k -- knit"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "p -- purl"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "m1r -- make one right (increase)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k2tog -- knit two together, right-leaning decrease"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ssk -- slip, slip, knit, left-leaning decrease"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Before you cast on, circle your size -- every count reads S (M, L)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on the 4 mm needle, cast on 116 (120, 128) sts using long-tail cast-on. Tail formula: tail_cm = (needle mm x stitch count) / 10 + 15. For size L on a 4 mm needle: (4 x 128) / 10 + 15 = 66 cm; round up to 72 cm. Join without twisting, place BOR marker."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work in stocking stitch until hat measures 12 cm from cast-on edge. After completing the crown body, you should have 116 (120, 128) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown shaping"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Place 8 markers dividing the work into 8 sections."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Decrease round 1: *k to 2 sts before marker, k2tog; repeat from * 8 times. 108 (112, 120) sts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: knit all."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue alternating decrease and plain rounds until 32 sts remain, then decrease every round until 8 sts remain."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After the final decrease round, you should have 8 stitches on the needle. Cut yarn, draw through all 8, pull up, and fasten on the inside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With right side facing and 4 mm needle, pick up and knit 116 (120, 128) sts around the cast-on edge. Join, place BOR marker. Work 2 plain rounds. Increase round: *k9, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "make-one"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "m1r"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "; repeat from * to end. To work m1r: lift the horizontal strand between the stitch on the right needle and the stitch on the left needle from front to back; knit through the back loop. This closes the lifted strand into a new stitch without a hole. Repeat the increase round every 4 rounds, working 2 plain rounds between each increase round, until the brim measures 9 cm. Switch to 3.5 mm needle. Cast off loosely."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim flops or sags in warm weather: wool brim in cotton yarn behaves differently; cotton holds firm, wool relaxes. If the pattern is knitted in wool, add a thin millinery wire inside the cast-off edge to hold the brim shape."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim edge is ruffled: increases are spaced too close together. Space each increase round at least 4 plain rounds apart and check the brim lies flat before continuing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pick-up edge shows gaps: stitches picked up too far from the cast-on edge. Pick up through both legs of each cast-on stitch at a consistent rate of 1 st per stitch."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Starch lightly or block over a wide plate to set the brim flat. Allow to dry completely."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash cool. Reshape the brim over a plate while damp and allow to dry fully. Do not tumble dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The knitted beret uses a similar increase-outward structure for the crown disc before the fabric folds down over the head."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}